Initialize git-hop repository structure with interactive setup for worktree conversion.

Converting a standard repository prompts for a structure. Scripts and
other non-interactive callers should pass --no-prompt, which selects the
recommended bare repo + worktrees conversion without asking; add
--regular for a regular repo + worktrees instead. Without --no-prompt, a
run with nothing readable on stdin fails rather than waiting for an
answer that will never come.

Committed .git-hop/hooks/ scripts are mirrored into the user's hopspace
when init succeeds; control via --hooks (symlink|copy|prompt|none).
See docs/hooks.md for details.

Usage:
  git-hop init [flags]

Aliases:
  init, setup, install

Flags:
  -n, --dry-run           Show conversion steps without executing
      --enable-chdir      Install shell integration for automatic directory switching after hop commands
      --force             Convert even with uncommitted changes (DANGEROUS; a backup is still taken); with --restore, move what occupies the original location aside (never deleted)
  -h, --help              help for init
      --hooks string      mirror committed .git-hop/hooks/ into hopspace: symlink|copy|prompt|none (overrides --no-hooks)
      --hooks-overwrite   overwrite an existing hopspace hook with different content (symlink/copy modes)
      --keep-backup       Preserve backup after successful conversion (default: hop.backup.keepBackup)
      --no-hooks          Skip hooks: no .git-hop/hooks/ directory, no lifecycle hook runs
      --no-prompt         Skip the interactive menu and convert non-interactively (bare unless --regular)
      --regular           Convert to a regular repo + worktrees instead of bare (with --no-prompt)
      --restore string    Restore a conversion backup to the location it was taken from (manual rollback)

Global Flags:
  -c, --config stringArray   config file (default is $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/git-hop/config.json) or key=value override (repeatable)
      --format string        Output format (csv, human, json, table, text, yaml) (default "table")
  -g, --global               use global hopspace in $GIT_HOP_DATA_HOME (default: local)
      --json                 output in JSON format
      --no-color             Disable ANSI color
      --no-hints             Suppress next-step hints after command output
      --offline              Disable network access. Highest-precedence override: flips off per-command network opt-ins (peer discovery, sync, GitHub, push). Enforced beneath net/http and any client routed through netpolicy.GuardDial; loopback and diagnostics stay exempt.
      --porcelain            machine-readable output
  -q, --quiet                Suppress non-essential output
  -V, --verbose count        Increase log verbosity (-V=debug, -VV=trace)
